{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers country-wise and level-wise counts of foreign students in India, based on actual responses. It tracks enrolment of foreign students by education level—All level, M.Phil., Ph.D., post graduate and under graduate—disaggregated by male and female. These indicators support analysis of international student participation and gender distribution across higher education levels. The data are published by the Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education, for use in planning, monitoring and research on higher education mobility.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers coverage under the Swavalamban Scheme, a co-contributory pension initiative for India’s unorganised sector. It focuses on subscribers enrolled through aggregators appointed under the Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA), including entities such as public sector banks, regional rural banks and private entities. The information supports tracking scheme participation and understanding the aggregator ecosystem for enrolment and contributions. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Financial Services.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Pension Reforms"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on COVID-19 patient information for Indore, covering cases reported through input hospitals under the Smart Cities Mission. It supports monitoring of COVID-19 burden at the city level and can be used for public health reporting, situational awareness, and analysis of patient trends. The work is associated with the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and relevant Smart Cities Mission entities in Madhya Pradesh. Data are organized around hospital-reported COVID-19 patients in Indore.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Crime in India compiles annual crime statistics for India from 1953 to 2023 across 67 editions. It covers cognizable crimes registered, IPC crimes and Local & Special Law cases, including major offences such as murder, culpable homicide, kidnapping & abduction, rape, robbery, dacoity and theft. The catalog also includes details on complaints received and cases registered, victims, property stolen and recovered, and aspects of court processes and trial periods. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB), it supports research, policy analysis and monitoring of crime trends.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 2001 data on Institutional Households by Household Size for India and its States. It supports analysis of how institutional households are distributed across different household-size categories, useful for demographic profiling and planning. The datasets are published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, drawing on Census enumeration outputs.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Road transport statistics for India covering the period 1970-71 to 2001-2002 across multiple editions. The datasets compile indicators on registered motor vehicles, road accidents including persons killed and injured, and infrastructure such as length of national highways. They also track driver and conductor licences and the physical and financial performance of State Road Transport Undertakings, along with revenue realised from road transport. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways for monitoring transport activity, safety, and sector performance.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Non Workers by Main Activity, Age and Sex presents Census-based counts of non-workers across India, with breakdowns by age and sex and by main activity categories such as students, household duties, dependents, retired persons/rentiers, pensioners, beggars and vagrants. It supports demographic and labour-force participation analysis by comparing patterns across the Census 1991, Census 2001 and Census 2011 editions. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Tracks the number of newly registered motor vehicles and the total number of registered motor vehicles across 35 States/UTs. Vehicle counts are organized by transport versus non-transport categories, supporting analysis of fleet growth and registration trends. Useful for transport planning, policy monitoring, and infrastructure and regulatory decision-making. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the catalog supports state/UT-level comparisons of motor vehicle registration activity.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers solid waste management for Chennai, Tamil Nadu, focusing on how municipal waste is handled from source segregation to door-to-door collection and onward processing and disposal. It brings together information on bin placement and sizes, collection vehicle types and capacities, and measures of collection efficiency. The scope supports planning and monitoring of sanitation services, including waste processing and options for waste collected from households. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and the Smart Cities Mission, with involvement from Tamil Nadu and Chennai.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Municipal Waste, Water and Sanitation; Sanitation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Union Budget editions 2018-19, 2021-22, 2022-23 and 2023-24 present India’s annual financial statement under Article 112 of the Constitution. The catalog brings together budget estimates and related fiscal information on receipts and expenditure, including revenue and capital components, taxes, subsidies, and deficit measures, along with revised figures where applicable. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, it supports analysis of fiscal policy, allocation trends, and budgetary planning for government, researchers, and policy stakeholders.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Union Budget: 2019-20 (Interim) brings together the interim Union Budget documents and related financial statements for India. It covers key budget aggregates such as receipts and expenditure, along with deficit-related indicators used to assess fiscal balance and funding priorities. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, the catalog supports analysis by policymakers, researchers, and citizens tracking government finances for the 2019-20 (Interim) period.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Village/Town-wise Primary Census Abstract provides 2011 census statistics for 34 States/UTs, covering households, population by age (including 0–6), and social composition such as Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe. It also includes literacy and work participation, with breakdowns of total workers into main and marginal workers and categories of cultivators, agricultural labourers, household industry workers, and other workers. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, it supports planning, demographic analysis, and socio-economic research at village and town level.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}
